resolved.question_text_html:
Fill in the blanks to define a valid dictionary with two elements.
[!raw!]
cars = {
   "BMW"{0} "blue"{1} 
   "Volvo": "red"{2}

resolved.description:
[s0l0!-header][h1]Dictionaries[/h1][/s0l0!-header]

You can use strings, integers, booleans, and any other [b]immutable[/b] type as dictionary keys.
This means that you cannot use lists or dictionaries as keys:[code format="py" codeId="361"]bad_dict = {
  [1, 2, 3]: "one two three", 
}[/code]
[note]The code above will generate an error, as it tries to use a list as the key.[/note]

